    "standardized_narrative": "Syndicate 33 reported a gross release of $398.1 million in prior year reserves, representing a 10.83% release of its opening gross claims outstanding. This favorable development was primarily driven by strong favorable development on prior-year losses and releases on older year catastrophe losses, including positive development on COVID-19 related claims. The Syndicate also benefited from improved underwriting results and rate and attritional loss improvements. However, the overall result was impacted by foreign exchange losses and mark-to-market investment losses due to increasing bond yields and aggressive central bank policy actions. The Syndicate also completed two legacy portfolio transfers to secure coverage for potential adverse development on historical liabilities, particularly in casualty and run-off classes.",
